1
00:00:00,583 --> 00:00:01,913
(Penny:)That is not true.

2
00:00:01,917 --> 00:00:03,587
(Amy:)I'm still waiting
on my mini corndogs

3
00:00:03,586 --> 00:00:05,756
(Amy:)from two years ago.

4
00:00:05,755 --> 00:00:09,125
(Penny:)I told you,
they'll be right out.

5
00:00:10,092 --> 00:00:12,762
(Amy:)Okay, so no
Bernadette.

6
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:15,262
(Penny:)Well, you saw her the
other night. Am I wrong?

7
00:00:15,264 --> 00:00:16,534
(Amy:)No, I just...

8
00:00:16,532 --> 00:00:19,332
(Amy:)I feel kind of uncomfortable
talking about her like this.

9
00:00:19,335 --> 00:00:22,305
(Amy:)Usually when someone's being
talked about behind their back,

10
00:00:22,304 --> 00:00:25,144
(Amy:)it's me and it's right
in front of my face.

11
00:00:25,141 --> 00:00:28,271
I-I'm sorry. I just need
a little break from her.

12
00:00:28,277 --> 00:00:30,377
(Amy:)I understand.

13
00:00:30,379 --> 00:00:34,349
(Amy:)You know, there is
some research that indicates

14
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:37,550
(Amy:)that sharing negative attitudes
about a third party

15
00:00:37,553 --> 00:00:40,523
(Amy:)can be a powerful bonding force
between two friends.

16
00:00:42,124 --> 00:00:43,524
(Penny:)So, what are
you saying?

17
00:00:43,526 --> 00:00:46,226
(Amy:)I'm saying,
in the spirit of science,

18
00:00:46,228 --> 00:00:48,528
(Sheldon:)what is
that little skank's problem?

19
00:00:52,201 --> 00:00:54,401
(Raj:)So, I've been trying
to come up

20
00:00:54,403 --> 00:00:56,303
(Raj:)with a cute couple's nickname
for me and Emily.

21
00:00:56,305 --> 00:00:57,935
(Raj:)What do you
like better--

22
00:00:57,940 --> 00:01:01,240
(Raj:)Emippali...

